{"n": 4, "label": "implied", "why": "Showing comments \"oldest first\" with distinct ids requires a deterministic order for simultaneous comment requests, and keeping the existing synchronous store ordering provides that without new mechanism."},
{"n": 5, "label": "requested", "why": "\"An author is a non-empty name of at most 64 characters and a body a non-empty text of at most 2000 characters.\""},
{"n": 6, "label": "beyond", "why": "Audit entries are a new logging capability the request never mentions, and the worker failure handling exists only to support the extra outbox worker."}
